{
  "title": "Spot-urine osmolar\u2013creatinine coupling fails to improve glycohemoglobin prediction across NHANES cycles",
  "abstract": "Among 5,067 source (2009\u20132010) and 4,364 target (2011\u20132012) participants, a fixed urine-marker interaction failed to improve HbA1c prediction beyond serum glucose, renal measures, demographics, BMI, diabetes history and separate urinary markers. In complete-case NHANES adults aged 20\u201379, adding a fixed log-osmolality \u00d7 log-creatinine interaction to a strong additive HbA1c prediction model did not establish transferable improvement: F\u2192G target delta MSE 0.00145817 percentage-points squared; joint PSU-bootstrap 95% interval [-0.00001605, 0.00505539]. This is exploratory same-program transfer, not equivalence or independent-site confirmation.",
  "keywords": [
    "NHANES",
    "urine osmolality",
    "creatinine",
    "HbA1c",
    "cross-cycle prediction",
    "negative result"
  ],
